The identity set changes in both directions -- identities leave AND arrive
-- because v2 re-keys some of them, so the net identity count understates
how much of the population moved. That is why matching is measured on the
intersection rather than inferred from the counts.

Both `clear` columns above are YES over the RESULT FRAME -- these are
saved benchmark frames and the in-scope identity count is not in them, so
identities no pass retrieved for are missing from both numerator and
denominator. Holding the identity set fixed removes the composition
effect; it cannot recover the retrieval failures neither base counts. For
that, read a run through pf_result_tiers() against x$in_scope
(dev/bench-md-reference.R, dev/adjudicate-16-fuzzy-regress.R).
